# Line endings are not cosmetic in this repository.
#
# The design corpus under docs/ contains ASCII wireframes and layered-architecture
# diagrams whose alignment was measured character-by-character during review
# (docs/08 §4.5, §7.4; docs/07 §3.2). A CRLF rewrite on checkout shifts byte
# offsets and silently breaks those checks. P0-T01 hit this — git warned that
# core.autocrlf would rewrite the corpus — and could only fix it for one working
# copy. This file fixes it for every clone, on every platform, with no local
# git configuration required.
#
# Last matching pattern wins, so the binary rules at the bottom override the
# text rules above them.

# Default: store LF in the object database, check LF out everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Recorded API responses (docs/07 §2.2, docs/13 §3). The record/replay layer
# compares these byte-for-byte, so a fixture recorded on Windows and one
# recorded on Linux must be identical. Never let git re-encode them.
test/fixtures/** text eol=lf

# Explicit only where auto-detection is genuinely uncertain. Common text types
# (.md, .ts, .js, .json, .xhtml, .css, .yml) are left to `text=auto` above: git
# never mis-detects them, and an explicit rule here would report `text: set`
# where this card's acceptance criterion expects `text: auto`.
#
# Fluent localization files carry an uncommon extension and a UTF-8 BOM-less
# convention; state it rather than rely on detection.
*.ftl   text eol=lf

# Binary — git must never re-encode or diff these.
# Plugin icons (addon/content/icons/, docs/13 §1.3's manifest entries):
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.svg   text eol=lf

# The IMRaD fixture corpus (P3-T20) and any packaged build output:
*.pdf   binary
*.xpi   binary
*.zip   binary

# Generated or recorded audio (docs/04):
*.wav   binary
*.mp3   binary

# Fonts, if any are ever vendored:
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
